<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/beijing" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/beijing.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-21">21 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Richard Nixon arrives in Beijing</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Nixon became the first US President to visit the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a>, meeting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mao-zedong">Mao Zedong</a>. His week-long trip ended more than two decades of hostility and reshaped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cold-war">Cold War</a> diplomacy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-2">2 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">J. Edgar Hoover dies after 48 years leading the FBI</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">J. Edgar Hoover died in Washington, having led the Bureau and its predecessor since 1924. He built a modern federal police force but also used it to spy on activists and politicians.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-22">22 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Ceylon becomes the Republic of Sri Lanka</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A new constitution made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceylon">Ceylon</a> a republic, ending the British monarch's role as head of state, and adopted the name <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>. The island had become independent in 1948.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceylon">Ceylon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-17">17 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Five men are arrested in the Watergate building</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Burglars linked to President Nixon's re-election committee were caught inside the Democratic National Committee offices in Washington. The cover-up led to Nixon's resignation in 1974.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-23">23 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Nixon approves using the CIA to block the Watergate inquiry</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">In a taped conversation, Nixon agreed that the CIA should ask the FBI to halt its investigation. The release of this 'smoking gun' tape in August 1974 forced his resignation.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-5">5 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Palestinian gunmen seize Israeli athletes at the Munich Olympics</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-september">Black September</a> militants killed two members of the Israeli team and took nine hostage. All nine and a West German policeman died in a failed rescue at Fürstenfeldbruck airbase.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-accession-1972">Treaty of Accession 1972</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty of Accession 1972 was the agreement signed in Brussels on 22 January 1972 under which the United Kingdom, Ireland and Denmark joined the European Economic Community on 1 January 1973.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/ikiza">Ikiza</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Ikiza ('the Catastrophe') was a campaign of mass killings in Burundi in 1972, in which the Tutsi-dominated army and the ruling party's youth wing killed perhaps 100,000 to 300,000 Hutu.</p></div></li></ol></section>
